faqs:
- q: Do you do probate house clearance?
  a: We help the family sort, pack and move belongings, and move a surviving partner or relative. We are not a probate service or a house clearance firm, so we do not give legal advice or empty a property for disposal.
- q: How much does probate house clearance cost?
  a: Prices vary with the size of the property and how much it holds, and clearance firms usually quote by volume, so get at least two or three written quotes. Chayce does not clear properties for disposal, but our sorting, packing and moving help starts at {bronze}.
- q: What is after-death house clearance?
  a: It usually means emptying a loved one&rsquo;s home once the estate allows. Chayce helps with the sorting and with moving what the family keeps; a separate clearance firm can deal with what is left. Our guide to <a href="/blog/moving-after-probate-clearing-a-loved-ones-home/">moving after probate</a> sets out the steps.
- q: Can I clear a house before probate is granted?
  a: That is a question for the executor and the estate&rsquo;s solicitor. Belongings can form part of the estate, so check before anything is given away, sold or thrown out.
- q: Who is allowed to deal with the home after a death?
  a: Usually the executor named in the will, or an administrator if there is no will. Your solicitor or GOV.UK can confirm who has the authority in your case.
- q: Can you help a surviving husband, wife or partner move?
  a: Yes. We can run a downsize or a move closer to family with a dedicated coordinator, at a pace that suits them.
- q: What happens to items nobody wants?
  a: 'The family decides: keep, sell, donate or let go. We do not take bulk items away for disposal, but we can help plan donation.'
- q: Is the removal insured?
  a: Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.
- q: Do you work outside Northampton?
  a: Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange moves across the whole UK.
